# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() stops a sleeping strand tagged with that tag;
#         concurrent variants: stop before vs after strand starts sleeping.
# blocked: needs a `## host:` rewrite — on the line-at-a-time path the
#          sleeper never wakes whether it is stopped or not, so the fixture
#          would pass without testing anything
# matrix-row: tag-stop
#
# Reason (re-probed on the re-founded core):
#   The two blockers this fixture used to name are gone.  `{expr} & stmt`
#   parses inside a tag-scope body, and `echo` resolves unqualified from
#   any realm now that the Lobby is in every realm's prototype chain.
#
#   What remains is not a gap in the language, it is the wrong runner.  A
#   chunk runs until nothing is READY and then hands back, which is what
#   makes line-at-a-time input work at all; a strand parked on
#   sleep(100ms) is therefore still parked when the line returns.  So
#   `echo("No")` is absent from the output EITHER WAY — with the stop and
#   without it.  Activating the fixture as written would produce a green
#   result that proves nothing, which is the one outcome worse than a
#   placeholder.
#
#   The rewrite it wants is the host driver: `## host: run` the tag scope,
#   `## host: advance-clock 200`, `## host: step`, and assert that nothing
#   was echoed — against a control that advances the clock with no stop
#   and DOES see the echo.
#
# Original urbiscript (kept for the rewrite):
# # var tag = Tag.new()
# # tag: { {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} & tag.stop() };
# # tag: { tag.stop() & {sleep(100ms); echo("No")} };
